  "live_records": {
    "q-126777": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126777",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{5}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{7}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+25\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+49\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
