    "q-143821": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143821",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{12}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{5}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{5}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{5}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each cubed value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{5}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{12}+{1}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+{2}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{5}{12}+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+32\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}+8 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
