    "q-143825": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143825",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.35$ | $0.4$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{4}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of ${X}^{4}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={1}^{4}\\cdot 0.25+{2}^{4}\\cdot 0.35+{3}^{4}\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+16\\cdot 0.35+81\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.25+5.6+32.4 \\\\  & =38.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
